course: dictionary
lesson: 2995
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The dictionary lists them, and the context tells you which one fits. Read the words around the word: they are its clues. «Mei's family folds dumplings together on New Year's Eve» tells you dumplings are food you make with your hands, so this meaning is the food.
explain: A dumpling is a small ball of dough that is boiled, steamed or fried, often with meat or vegetables inside. To check your meaning, put it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you are probably right.
explain: The same word can also be a fond name. Some people call a small, chubby child or pet a dumpling, as a loving nickname. Read the whole sentence to see which meaning the writer means.
fact: A dumpling is a small ball of dough that is boiled, steamed or fried.
fact: Dumplings can be filled with meat or vegetables, as in «stew and dumplings».
fact: An apple dumpling is a pudding of fruit wrapped in pastry.
fact: Informally, «dumpling» is a fond name for a small, chubby child or pet.
fact: Dumplings come from many food cultures: jiaozi (China), pierogi (Poland), varenyky (Ukraine) and gyoza (Japan).
exercise: «The family folds dumplings together on New Year's Eve.» What are the dumplings? | A famous dance | A cuddly toy | A pudding of apples in pastry | *Small balls of dough cooked to eat
exercise: «Dessert was an apple dumpling, wrapped in pastry.» Which meaning is this? | A fond name for a child | A small ball of dough in a soup | A kind of cake | *A pudding of fruit wrapped in pastry
exercise: Mum calls her baby «my little dumpling». What does dumpling mean here? | A baby's cot | *A fond name for a small, chubby child | A small ball of dough | A pudding of apples in pastry
test: «Babcia sends Olga a recipe for pierogi (dumplings).» What kind of food are pierogi? | *A kind of dumpling, a filled ball of dough | A type of tea | A kind of dance | A fruit pudding only
test: In «steamed dumplings», what does steamed mean? | Filled with meat | Fried in hot oil | Cut into small pieces | *Cooked in hot steam
exam: Which sentence uses dumpling as a fond name for a small, chubby child? | «Dumplings are popular at Chinese New Year.» | «The stew had two big dumplings.» | *«Come and have a cuddle, my little dumpling!»
